    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28086" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marrŭbĭum</span></b>  or
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marrŭvĭum</span></b> , ii,
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				city in Latium, the capital of the Marsians</i>, now <i>S. Benedetto</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			507</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marrŭbĭus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Marrubium, Marrubian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marrubia gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 750</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marrŭvĭi</span></b>  or
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Marrŭvīni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Marrubium</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 12,
				17, § 106</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Inscr.
				Orell. 3149</span></i>.</div>
